Alex (docs): Thinking we should add a small flowchart to the error-ref page that shows the fallback order for 429s/timeouts/context limits. Right now the prose is confusing and folks keep asking which fallback runs first.
Maria (eng-runtime): +1. A visual would help. Could we do a tiny SVG or Mermaid block and embed it? Keeps it stable across docs builds. :ok_hand:
Sanjay (eng-ml): Current runtime behavior (for reference): 1) client retry w/backoff 2) middleware fallback (trim/context clip or summarize) 3) model variant downgrade (smaller model / quantized) 4) regional fallback. We should annotate triggers: 429 vs request timeout vs queue-depth/backpressure.
Tim (devex): I'll draft as Mermaid. Example to iterate on:```mermaid
flowchart LR
  Req[Request] --> Type{Error type?}
  Type -- 429 --> Retry[Client retry + backoff]
  Type -- timeout --> Trim[Trim/summarize & retry]
  Retry --> Still[Still throttled?]
  Still -- yes --> ModelDown[Fallback: smaller model / quantized]
  ModelDown --> Region[Regional failover]
  Still -- no --> Success[Success]
```
Alex (docs): Great. Add small callouts for headers to check: `Retry-After`, `X-Request-ID`, and `X-Sequence-Id` for streaming continuity. Also add a short paragraph about when to prefer client-side retry vs server-side fallback.
Maria (eng-runtime): Note: for streaming requests 'retry' semantics differ. We should call out that streaming idempotency must be preserved (reconnect with resume token or failover to resumable session). I'll add a short bullet in the doc.
Sanjay (eng-ml): Also include a tiny example about KV cache compatibility when switching to quantized models—some quantized kernels change key sizes. Suggest: attempt to reuse cache; if mismatch, fall back to cold-start and document expected latency bump.
Tim (devex): I'll add SDK snippets (JS + Python). JS will show Retry-After parsing + exponential backoff with decorrelated jitter. Python will be a minimal retry helper with circuit-breaker note.
Alex (docs): Ownership: I'll open the PR with the mermaid block + prose + link fixes (there are some stale runbook URLs). @Tim add the snippets in that PR, @Maria please sanity-check the fallback triggers and add a test in infra that simulates 429 cascades.
Tim (devex): Working on snippets. Draft JS example:```js
async function safeFetch(req, retries=4){
  for(let i=0;i<retries;i++){
    const res = await fetch(req);
    if(res.status===429){
      const ra = parseInt(res.headers.get('Retry-After')||'0',10);
      const wait = ra>0 ? ra*1000 : Math.min(60000, (2**i)*100 + Math.random()*100);
      await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r, wait));
      continue;
    }
    return res;
  }
  throw new Error('retry-failed');
}
```
Sanjay (eng-ml): I'll drop a short snippet showing `trim_to_window()` pseudo-code for middleware that preserves instruction tokens.
Alex (docs): I've opened PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4123 - includes initial flowchart and a section stub for SDK snippets. docs-bot: PR created by Alex (docs).
docs-bot: New PR note - label: docs, scope: error-ref, reviewers requested: eng-runtime, devex.
Maria (eng-runtime): I'll review tomorrow. If the Mermaid looks too simplistic we can convert it to a state machine diagram and move to the infra runbook. Also will add a comment about queue-depth thresholds that trigger regional failover.
Tim (devex): ETA for snippets: Thursday EOD. I'll try to include both fetch + SDK-friendly wrappers.
Alex (docs): Plan: merge after Tim's snippets and Maria signoff. If no blockers aim for EOD Friday. I'll include a changelog entry for the release notes.
Sanjay (eng-ml): One last ask: include a short FAQ line: "If I see 429s intermittently, should I always retry?" Answer: "Start with client retry + backoff; if 429s persist, enable middleware trim or a smaller model; open a support ticket if persistent across days."
Alex (docs): Perfect. Thanks all. I'll add the FAQ and ping when PR is ready for review.
